# Review

## Summary

The note imports several concepts: selection-based learning, scheduler–LLM separation, semantic-work relocation, operative change, diagnostic richness and criterion revision. It applies them to its proposed split. The footer relation labels (defined-in, grounds, extends) make clear which concepts are inherited and which the note applies, and the note's own contribution is clearly the three-competence decomposition. The two parenthetical citations on competences 1 and 2 compress a concept and its object of application, but context resolves both, so neither meets the materiality threshold.
